{
  "description": "deixis mandatory Node[T] parts, contexts and cuts — decompose/compose of ADR 0010 §3, split/plug, replacement and cut/rebuild of §4 and PATH.md. decompose's result is {\"parts\": {\"own\": …, \"children\": […]}}. A context or skeleton is a node spelling with {\"hole\": {}} in place of each removed subtree. split's result is {\"defined\": {\"context\": …, \"subtree\": …}}, and cut's is {\"defined\": {\"skeleton\": …, \"subtrees\": [[path, node], …]}}; each is {\"undefined\": {}} outside its domain. Every case declares its slot. Hand-authored from docs/design/0010-mandatory-node-values.md, docs/TREE.md and docs/PATH.md as merged in 1a9bb6d, and from nothing else. No implementation of the mandatory API existed when these were written. Items X2, X3 and X11–X13; each note names the defect (W) it catches. op \"replace\" with a \"then\" field replaces twice at the same path. 26 cases.",
